-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:08:00-08:00","id":1056698,"title":"","content":"<br /> I guess I'll have to agree.<br /> Considering spirits can do the fetich thing by themselves, my other ideas for why this could work all sound terrible.<br /> <br /> Prime 4 for spirits with low self esteem who don't believe in their own capabilities, tsundere spirits who are willing to become fetiches but not willing, and spirits with Fetichtile dysfunction...<br /> <br /> Chiminage (and making a fetich using spirit 2) isn't actually mentioned in M20 as far as i know though, so it might be considered valid only if you take the rulebook by itself... which is obviously not how we want to use mage, and even then, the logic is flimsy.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, maybe someone just made a mistaken copy paste or something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:11:35-08:00","id":1056700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1056630#post1056630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's unnecessary. It means that Spirit mages would be required to have Prime 4 if they wanted to have constant spirit companions.<br /> This is new to M20 and should be quite promptly ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, why would you be required to have it? It's not noted as an extra requirement. It's an alternative method. (albeit a bad one that makes no sense)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:30:30-08:00","id":1056703,"title":"","content":"Prime to Bind the spirit makes sense because you are creating a magical Object. In werewolf you can't just ask a spirit to go into an object to make a Fetish, you perform the Rite of the Fetish. Mages aren't using Garou Rites so they have to weave their own magic which bridges the Spirits Fetish Home and their effects upon the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:26:07-08:00","id":1056729,"title":"","content":"But I thought the spirits could do this themselves? Or is this a contradiction between books?<br /> On that note, why would this (Prime 4) only work on a willing spirit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T20:25:34-08:00","id":1057422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1056606#post1056606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The willing spirit goes into the item and then you use prime 4 to meld the patterns together by solidifying and making more real the reality of the oneness of spirit &amp; item with copious use of the stuff of magick maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what spirit is for so you don't need prime, the spirit provides it's own &quot;juice&quot; to power the fetish in the form of the spirits own essence( which is where the Chiminage comes in, if you anger the spirit it decides it doesn't feel like working that day) , you need prime to make a magical object because it doesn't have that being of energy inside to make it magical.<br /> <br /> Think of it as putting water in a jar, with the spirit being the water. With the spirit sphere you just put it in there and you have a fetish.<br /> <br /> Now say you don't have a spirit or putting spirits into things just isn't your style then you use prime. Now the water is quintessence which you create with prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 03-02-2017, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T00:40:00-08:00","id":1057964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1056703#post1056703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime to Bind the spirit makes sense because you are creating a magical Object. In werewolf you can't just ask a spirit to go into an object to make a Fetish, you perform the Rite of the Fetish. Mages aren't using Garou Rites so they have to weave their own magic which bridges the Spirits Fetish Home and their effects upon the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rite of the fetish in Werewolf is NOT a magical power, but rather, its a religious ritual, made to properly adress the spirit. The process of Chiminage for mages is exactly the same thing, it will require a series of proper ways to adress the spirit, fitting oferings, and all the cerimonial involved. Its just that Mage dont have the same mechanics as Werewolf do.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you wanna simply go beyond all that, just use Spirit 4 and trap the damn thing, period. See, its not Prime that it is used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T01:31:20-08:00","id":1057968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1057422#post1057422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what spirit is for so you don't need prime, the spirit provides it's own &quot;juice&quot; to power the fetish in the form of the spirits own essence( which is where the Chiminage comes in, if you anger the spirit it decides it doesn't feel like working that day) , you need prime to make a magical object because it doesn't have that being of energy inside to make it magical.<br /> <br /> Think of it as putting water in a jar, with the spirit being the water. With the spirit sphere you just put it in there and you have a fetish.<br /> <br /> Now say you don't have a spirit or putting spirits into things just isn't your style then you use prime. Now the water is quintessence which you create with prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to make it clear, I'm simply trying to find any plausible reason (other than typo or lapse in judgement) for use of Prime 4 as an alternative (I'm not sure people are getting that it is an alternative and not an additional requirement) to Spirit 4 for a &quot;willing spirit&quot;, and only as an academic exercise because this is mentioned in the books. I understand how the normal processes work. Though I do understand my posits are somewhat flimsy in the light of chiminage. My next proposal is that Prime 4 could help a mage with a willing spirit who does not understand the rites of chiminage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-04-2017, 04:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T02:39:29-08:00","id":1057976,"title":"","content":"1: all spirits understand chiminage, it's intrinsic.<br /> <br /> 2: without spirit how are you even dealing with a spirit? it's like trying to make fire without forces or heal without life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T05:07:39-08:00","id":1058001,"title":"","content":"That's a good point. You need Spirit 2 to even reach across the Gauntlet, the same sphere rating required to perform chiminage (you know, for talking). So if you need Soirit 2 to interact with spirits with Prime, why then would you use Prime 4 to bind them when you could just talk to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T11:33:35-08:00","id":1058102,"title":"","content":"I just took a new look on Spirit Ways... It says just that you need Spirit 2 for Chiminage, but it doesn't say anything about the spirits being able to &quot;possess&quot; an item by their own; and to make matters worse, it says you need Spirit 4 to make fetishes.<br /> <br /> Now, I really dont know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T13:53:49-08:00","id":1058134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058102#post1058102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just took a new look on Spirit Ways... It says just that you need Spirit 2 for Chiminage, but it doesn't say anything about the spirits being able to &quot;possess&quot; an item by their own; and to make matters worse, it says you need Spirit 4 to make fetishes.<br /> <br /> Now, I really dont know</div> </div> </div> </div>Read Axis Mundi for how Chiminage works. Literally any spirit can chose to bind themselves to a fetish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:17:51-08:00","id":1058207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1057976#post1057976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1: all spirits understand chiminage, it's intrinsic.<br /> <br /> 2: without spirit how are you even dealing with a spirit? it's like trying to make fire without forces or heal without life.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Oh, sorry; I meant the mage didn't understand chiminage.<br /> 2. No good reason really. It's like attempting to heal someone with Time just to see if you can (or trying to raise a sunken boat using ping pong balls or something like that).<br /> <br /> But yes, I understand I'm pretty much grasping at straws at this point. I was just hoping someone could help me come up with something so I can tell my players &quot;This is what this is for&quot; rather than &quot;Oh, just ignore that part&quot;. That's all really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-04-2017, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T17:42:46-08:00","id":1058216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058207#post1058207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Oh, sorry; I meant the mage didn't understand chiminage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why are they messing around with spirits without a lick of knowledge or spheres?<br /> <br /> Look at the prime section on M20 p.520-521. <br /> Say you want to drain a spirit of its essence you still need spirit (it's a prime 4/spirit 4 thing).<br /> <br /> You still need spirit 2 to talk to the darn thing and prime 4 to make it to a fetish if it's willing M20 p.508. If it's not then you need spirit 4 to cram it into what ever you want.<br /> <br /> I would suggest looking at the werewolf book Hammer and claive, it's got a great section on how someone goes around making a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T18:27:43-08:00","id":1058233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058216#post1058216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why are they messing around with spirits without a lick of knowledge or spheres?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because an absurd hypothetical casper the friendly spirit came along and the idiot mage thought, he's willing to be my fetich, I don't get this chiminage bit. Maybe I'll do this the way I know how? <br /> <br /> I'm talking hypothetical doing things because maybe you can (I'm not saying you actually could in this case)<br /> As I mentioned, I'm thinking in the zone of terrible ideas and weird methods. Not practicality or common sense.<br /> <br /> The same way you could light a fire with a match, two sticks, a fire piston, wires and a car battery, and making a lighting rod and holding it in the proper manner to send a spark into something flammable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058216#post1058216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at the prime section on M20 p.520-521.<br /> Say you want to drain a spirit of its essence you still need spirit (it's a prime 4/spirit 4 thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm just looking for a plausible explanation of what's in the book (make a fetich using Prime 4 for a willing spirit) more than actual logical consistency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058216#post1058216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You still need spirit 2 to talk to the darn thing and prime 4 to make it to a fetish if it's willing M20 p.508. If it's not then you need spirit 4 to cram it into what ever you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the spirit already has the powers to talk to you but is just bad at explaining itself. Again, I just want to be able to tell my players &quot;This is what this is for&quot; rather than &quot;Oh, just ignore that part&quot;.<br /> <br /> I do honestly hope I'm not irritating you with this nonsense. This will probably never come up in a game I run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058216#post1058216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest looking at the werewolf book Hammer and claive, it's got a great section on how someone goes around making a fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't access to the werewolf books though. Only several mage books and a few vampire ones. While I do try to get as many of these books as I can, it feels odd to have to reference a werewolf book for what is essentially a mage problem and specifically a mage m20 problem.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T05:54:44-08:00","id":1058373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058134#post1058134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Read Axis Mundi for how Chiminage works. Literally any spirit can chose to bind themselves to a fetish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im really not trying to be combative (I'll look axis mundi soon, I just hadn't have the time), but isn't axis mundi a Werewolf book from the era they hadn't yet incorporate the high Umbra from Mage? Could it be that this is an ability intrinsic only to spirits from the middle Umbra, not to high umbrood (the most common sorts that hermetics and choristers deal with)<br /> <br /> Oh, and what about wraiths? (Or even specters, if you dig the thrill of constantly risking your soul hubristic bending the will of monsters of utter doom). I dont think they can, on their own accord, inhabit items in the material world without... I dont remember the name of the Arcanoi now, but there is one... Anyway, I guess wraiths would give access to their Arcanoi, correct? Except that, as wraiths are PERSONS (as in, human beings, just bad luck and kind of imaterial human beings) I can't really see a person thinking that its a bless to spend some decades trapped in a vodoo doll to be used by some point hat.<br /> <br /> Spirit ways thou does say that spirits, specially minor and weaker ones, love becoming fetishes. This gives them the opportunity to hide from the (literally) Umbral jungle, because weak spirits have a hard time to survive, plus, they get the chance to influence the material world and increase their knowledge AND being useful (fetishes will hate being left in a closet without use ever. They wanna be used). Another interesting thing I didn't knew is that many fetishes are <i>curious</i> and <i>talk a lot</i> (not all fetishes will be so social mind you, some will only talk when need, but the thing is, THEY TALK). I always assumed fetishes were just tools... A hammer for my nail problems.<br /> <br /> Actually, its far worse.<br /> <br /> Each fetish have a mind of its own (more than one some times). Yep... Im no longer so sure that those things really are worth it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T06:01:21-08:00","id":1058376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058373#post1058373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Im really not trying to be combative (I'll look axis mundi soon, I just hadn't have the time), but isn't axis mundi a Werewolf book from the era they hadn't yet incorporate the high Umbra from Mage? Could it be that this is an ability intrinsic only to spirits from the middle Umbra, not to high umbrood (the most common sorts that hermetics and choristers deal with)<br /> <br /> Oh, and what about wraiths? (Or even specters, if you dig the thrill of constantly risking your soul hubristic bending the will of monsters of utter doom). I dont think they can, on their own accord, inhabit items in the material world without... I dont remember the name of the Arcanoi now, but there is one... Anyway, I guess wraiths would give access to their Arcanoi, correct? Except that, as wraiths are PERSONS (as in, human beings, just bad luck and kind of imaterial human beings) I can't really see a person thinking that its a bless to spend some decades trapped in a vodoo doll to be used by some point hat.<br /> <br /> Spirit ways thou does say that spirits, specially minor and weaker ones, love becoming fetishes. This gives them the opportunity to hide from the (literally) Umbral jungle, because weak spirits have a hard time to survive, plus, they get the chance to influence the material world and increase their knowledge AND being useful (fetishes will hate being left in a closet without use ever. They wanna be used). Another interesting thing I didn't knew is that many fetishes are <i>curious</i> and <i>talk a lot</i> (not all fetishes will be so social mind you, some will only talk when need, but the thing is, THEY TALK). I always assumed fetishes were just tools... A hammer for my nail problems.<br /> <br /> Actually, its far worse.<br /> <br /> Each fetish have a mind of its own (more than one some times). Yep... Im no longer so sure that those things really are worth it</div> </div> </div> </div>Take a look at Forged by Dragons Fire. It talks about Hermetic Fetishes and how that works with Angels. No Prime required.<br /> <br /> As for Wraiths, I'd argue that you'd probably be able to use their Fetters as some form of Fetish. Only really applicable to wraiths with physical mobile objects as fetters. Also, Wraiths are not really useful spirits to keep around, because of their shadows they are much less predictable than standard spirits.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Fetish's aren't tools, they're more like speed dial. At any point (unless you use Spirit 4) a spirit can decide you're broken whatever agreement you have and just up and leave you, or worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T06:16:23-08:00","id":1058379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058233#post1058233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe because an absurd hypothetical casper the friendly spirit came along and the idiot mage thought, he's willing to be my fetich, I don't get this chiminage bit. Maybe I'll do this the way I know how? <br /> <br /> I'm talking hypothetical doing things because maybe you can (I'm not saying you actually could in this case)<br /> As I mentioned, I'm thinking in the zone of terrible ideas and weird methods. Not practicality or common sense.<br /> <br /> The same way you could light a fire with a match, two sticks, a fire piston, wires and a car battery, and making a lighting rod and holding it in the proper manner to send a spark into something flammable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again, I'm just looking for a plausible explanation of what's in the book (make a fetich using Prime 4 for a willing spirit) more than actual logical consistency.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe the spirit already has the powers to talk to you but is just bad at explaining itself. Again, I just want to be able to tell my players &amp;quot;This is what this is for&amp;quot; rather than &amp;quot;Oh, just ignore that part&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> I do honestly hope I'm not irritating you with this nonsense. This will probably never come up in a game I run.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I haven't access to the werewolf books though. Only several mage books and a few vampire ones. While I do try to get as many of these books as I can, it feels odd to have to reference a werewolf book for what is essentially a mage problem and specifically a mage m20 problem.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Forget that Prime 4 thing. Its just plain nonsense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T07:21:40-08:00","id":1058390,"title":"","content":"Axis mundi is for both games, although book of madness has a section on high power umbrood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:15:32-08:00","id":1058458,"title":"","content":"And now, Axis Mundi, page 37, says that spirits don't like being bounded to objects, and that they remain on a half-slumber state when in a fetish<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058390#post1058390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Axis mundi is for both games, although book of madness has a section on high power umbrood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Axis Mundi IS NOT a book for Mage, it is fully Werewolf the Apocalypse, althouth you can use it without fear (as long as it doesn't contradict other Mage's sources). It is a good book nevertheless, so it is a good reading for Mage either way (just couple it with Spirit Ways which is also great and a few others like Book of the Worlds, Infinite Tapestry and others. Oh, I just got my hands on Possessed for WtA, I loved that, specially the Drones)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T10:31:33-08:00","id":1058468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058458#post1058458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Axis Mundi IS NOT a book for Mage</div> </div> </div> </div>*looks at the cover of Axis Mundi, sees &quot;&amp; for Mage the Ascension&quot;. Looks at back cover sees Mage logo* totes not for mage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:37:44-08:00","id":1058501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058468#post1058468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*looks at the cover of Axis Mundi, sees &amp;quot;&amp; for Mage the Ascension&amp;quot;. Looks at back cover sees Mage logo* totes not for mage</div> </div> </div> </div>And looks at page 3, sees &quot;Legends of The Garou&quot; in its title, looks at the ENTIRE content, holds no simbol of Mage, no references of Mage, doesn't say a single line about spirit Sphere, while, in the other hand, does say A LOT about Garou interactions with spirits, dont even have the borders with the style of Mage books (they are all of WtA), and basically, the only thing that it has about Mages is the cover saying that you can use this book for Mages too.<br /> <br /> And yes, you can use it for Mage. But its NOT a Mage book - not even close to it.<br /> <br /> Another way at looking at this book is &quot;this is what Mage SHOULD be, under WtA&quot;.<br /> But, like I said, its a good book any way, so it doesn't really matter all that much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:13:06-08:00","id":1058533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058501#post1058501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And looks at page 3, sees &quot;Legends of The Garou&quot; in its title, looks at the ENTIRE content, holds no simbol of Mage, no references of Mage, doesn't say a single line about spirit Sphere, while, in the other hand, does say A LOT about Garou interactions with spirits, dont even have the borders with the style of Mage books (they are all of WtA), and basically, the only thing that it has about Mages is the cover saying that you can use this book for Mages too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... Let's ignore that entire side bar on Page 15 that literally says &quot;Using this book with Mage: The Ascension&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:14:20-08:00","id":1058534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058468#post1058468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*looks at the cover of Axis Mundi, sees &amp;quot;&amp; for Mage the Ascension&amp;quot;. Looks at back cover sees Mage logo* totes not for mage</div> </div> </div> </div>Axis Mundi, sidebar on page 15.<br /> <br /> In there, it says &quot;how to use this book with Mage the Ascension&quot;.<br /> <br /> It basically says it is NOT a book for Mage.<br /> <br /> And that sidebar alone already have many miscomceptions regarding Mage.<br /> <br /> It stats with all the letters that this book deals with the Middle Umbra and the &quot;Gaian spirits&quot;, not the spirits of the High Umbra, not Paradox spirits, and not the things from Mage.<br /> <br /> It also says that &quot;Gaian spirits are fixed; Paradox spirits usually will appear differently for each person looking at it&quot;.<br /> <br /> That would kind of solve the old problem between Mage x Werewolf of subjective x objective reality, just from the point of view of WtA. Not for Mage.<br /> <br /> However, like I said, Axis Mundi is a good fountain to drink upon, but it must be done with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> For Mage, its more apropriate to follow Spirit Ways, Book of Worlds, Book of Madness and Infinity Tapestry, those are indeed Mage sourcebooks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:25:04-08:00","id":1058540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058533#post1058533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah... Let's ignore that entire side bar on Page 15 that literally says &amp;quot;Using this book with Mage: The Ascension&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could just as much be: &quot;how to superimpose WtA lore over Mage scenario&quot;.<br /> <br /> The book is boringly (from a Mage view point) objective. Spirits are THAT. And that. And that.<br /> <br /> Thats NOT how it works for Mage. For Mage, spirits are whatever the hell they think they are.<br /> <br /> Take a look into Spirits Ways (thats really a book for Mages). It says that the VE Orange suits ARE there, is just that... They hate mid Umbra. They are just not so common there, because they hate all the suicidal maniac shapeshifters and all other RDs that infect this god forsaken jungle. <br /> This tiny sidebar on page 15 of Axis Mundi, one of the few mentions of mages in it, almost says that technomancers can't go to the middle Umbra, which is not even close to the truth.<br /> It gives the Werewolf version of an objective reality, saying that the spirits of mid umb are what they are. Spirit Ways however, will not endorse this.<br /> <br /> All in all, Axis Mundi is a book for Garou, and you can use it to use Mages in your WtA games, but it is NOT a book designed to be a sourcebook for Mage; still, it has many good stuff that can be used and considered nevertheless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:28:34-08:00","id":1058541,"title":"","content":"It would be like placing a sidebar on the Book of Worlds saying &quot;How to use this Book with Werewolf the Apocalypse&quot; and say &quot;Aha! See? Its a sourcebook for WtA!&quot;, which wouldn't be true at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:34:01-08:00","id":1058548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058534#post1058534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Axis Mundi, sidebar on page 15.<br /> <br /> In there, it says &quot;how to use this book with Mage the Ascension&quot;.<br /> <br /> It basically says it is NOT a book for Mage.<br /> <br /> And that sidebar alone already have many miscomceptions regarding Mage.<br /> <br /> It stats with all the letters that this book deals with the Middle Umbra and the &quot;Gaian spirits&quot;, not the spirits of the High Umbra, not Paradox spirits, and not the things from Mage.<br /> <br /> It also says that &quot;Gaian spirits are fixed; Paradox spirits usually will appear differently for each person looking at it&quot;.<br /> <br /> That would kind of solve the old problem between Mage x Werewolf of subjective x objective reality, just from the point of view of WtA. Not for Mage.<br /> <br /> However, like I said, Axis Mundi is a good fountain to drink upon, but it must be done with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> For Mage, its more apropriate to follow Spirit Ways, Book of Worlds, Book of Madness and Infinity Tapestry, those are indeed Mage sourcebooks</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, if you really want to be difficult about this, by all means interpret it that way.<br /> I rather think that the message implies that these Totem spirits and Naturae are the kind of spirits that are more specific to the Dreamspeakers and the Verbena, while the other traditions would be more at home with entities in the Astral Realm.<br /> <br /> That being said, Book of Worlds, Infinite Tapestry, and Book of Madness all suggest that one may be many and many may be one. For example, the Norns described in Axis Mundi. This is how they appear in the Spirit realm, but nothing says that we can't have them in the Astral Realm as well, perhaps as the Fates, or a different incarnation of the Norns. That being said, nothing says all these incarnations aren't just different faces of the same entity. Spirits do not abide by normal rules.<br /> <br /> Similarly, who's to say the Elementals seen in the Spirit Wilds are not members of the Elemental Court within the High Umbra? Things in the spirit world are as malleable as you wish them to be. If you really want to draw a line in the sand and say &quot;No, they're all different, Werewolf is for Werewolf and will never work in Mage&quot; then fine, so be it. Though such rigidity in my opinion is simply far too stifling.<br /> <br /> If instead you're going on the basis of &quot;Keep each book series separate for &quot;the one true way to play&quot;, then consider this:<br /> <br /> World of Darkness Tokyo is a Wraith book, but it has a bunch of stuff for Vampire, Mage, and Werewolf which you're unlikely to find anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Isle of the Mighty is a Changeling book, but it's the only source that talks in any length about the Harbingers of Avalon, a small faction of the Technocracy only vaguely mentioned in the Mage books.<br /> <br /> The Stats for Lunes and Pattern Spiders are in Mage 2nd as well as Book of Worlds.<br /> <br /> There is a great deal of room for overlap in all these areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T00:29:27-08:00","id":1058811,"title":"","content":"Here's how we've been handling it.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpirit 2 allows to you summon spirits and bargain with them. If the spirit is willing and has the Possession charm, it can enter an item and effectively become a fetish. The fetish doesn't have an owner and isn't specifically tied to the mage, but otherwise activates in the usual way. Of course, spirits with the Possession charm tend to be unpleasant, so be careful with your bargain.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpirit 4 is for binding an unwilling (or slumbering) spirit into a fetish. It forces them into the item and turns it into a fetish belonging to the caster. The spirit is likely to be unhappy unless the mage mollifies it somehow.<br /> <br /> \u200bPrime 4 is for a willing spirit. The Effect binds it to the object and turns it into a fetish belonging to the caster. So long as the caster keeps to their bargain with the spirit, all is fine.<br /> <br /> You can of course also use Spirit 4 to bind a willing spirit. Prime 4 is an overlap and workaround for mages who (for example) have Spirit 2 and can summon and bargain with a spirit, but lack Spirit 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:32:19-08:00","id":1058838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058548#post1058548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, if you really want to be difficult about this, by all means interpret it that way.<br /> I rather think that the message implies that these Totem spirits and Naturae are the kind of spirits that are more specific to the Dreamspeakers and the Verbena, while the other traditions would be more at home with entities in the Astral Realm.<br /> <br /> That being said, Book of Worlds, Infinite Tapestry, and Book of Madness all suggest that one may be many and many may be one. For example, the Norns described in Axis Mundi. This is how they appear in the Spirit realm, but nothing says that we can't have them in the Astral Realm as well, perhaps as the Fates, or a different incarnation of the Norns. That being said, nothing says all these incarnations aren't just different faces of the same entity. Spirits do not abide by normal rules.<br /> <br /> Similarly, who's to say the Elementals seen in the Spirit Wilds are not members of the Elemental Court within the High Umbra? Things in the spirit world are as malleable as you wish them to be. If you really want to draw a line in the sand and say &amp;quot;No, they're all different, Werewolf is for Werewolf and will never work in Mage&amp;quot; then fine, so be it. Though such rigidity in my opinion is simply far too stifling.<br /> <br /> If instead you're going on the basis of &amp;quot;Keep each book series separate for &amp;quot;the one true way to play&amp;quot;, then consider this:<br /> <br /> World of Darkness Tokyo is a Wraith book, but it has a bunch of stuff for Vampire, Mage, and Werewolf which you're unlikely to find anywhere else.<br /> <br /> Isle of the Mighty is a Changeling book, but it's the only source that talks in any length about the Harbingers of Avalon, a small faction of the Technocracy only vaguely mentioned in the Mage books.<br /> <br /> The Stats for Lunes and Pattern Spiders are in Mage 2nd as well as Book of Worlds.<br /> <br /> There is a great deal of room for overlap in all these areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont disagree, my only note is that it is primarily a Werewolf book, thats all. But I do think it is a good book, and it is very useful for Mage games. IF you take its content considering its original source.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <br /> -Axis Mundi says the spirits dont like being in fetishes, dont it only in the most dire situations (to hide from Umbral persecution, dire need, or generous offers)<br /> Spirit Ways (the book totally designed for Mage - and more specifically, for Shamans, both Dreamspeakers, the ocasional Verbena and others, even outside the Traditions), says that the spirits <i>desire</i> to become fetishes. This is a fate upon which most gafflings aspire to.<br /> <br /> -Axis Mundi say the fetishes remain in a semi slumber state<br /> -Spirit Ways say they talk to the owner.<br /> <br /> So, when considering those differences, we should adhere to the Mage source.<br /> The book is still very good with plenty of good stuff, we just must look at it with Mage's lenses<br /> <br /> What I think its fun, is that, while a book like Axis Mundi is a rich reading for Mage, as long as you take the care to mind some minor conflicts, mostly, books from Mage will be useless for WtA, because of the subjectivity of them.<br /> <br /> Oh, for this fetish part, I just looked at Hammer and Klaive, very good book too, but it brings out too many complications to the table. Besides, Werewolf work with &quot;f\u00f3rmulas&quot; (as in, common steps) - &quot;Go in a quest to find the materials, roll Allies, Contacs, etc after a week, manufacture the item, Wits + Craft after X days, purify it, Attribute + Skill. after X time with a ritual, call the spirit, Chiminage&quot; and so forth (also, it uses the Ritual ability, a trait exclusively to Fera). Thats rather limiting for the point of view of Mage - an Etherite scientist will make those steps, but in a very different way. And the rules dont need to be so overextensive either (fetishes are primary concerns to Werebeasts, but secondary in Mage). Still, it is a good source nonetheless (what I think it serves Mage the best, is to establish some reasoning behind the level of the Fetish background, and to give some ideas on what spirits to call for what, and what kind of object would fit with)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:47:50-08:00","id":1058843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058811#post1058811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how we've been handling it.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpirit 2 allows to you summon spirits and bargain with them. If the spirit is willing and has the Possession charm, it can enter an item and effectively become a fetish. The fetish doesn't have an owner and isn't specifically tied to the mage, but otherwise activates in the usual way. Of course, spirits with the Possession charm tend to be unpleasant, so be careful with your bargain.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpirit 4 is for binding an unwilling (or slumbering) spirit into a fetish. It forces them into the item and turns it into a fetish belonging to the caster. The spirit is likely to be unhappy unless the mage mollifies it somehow.<br /> <br /> \u200bPrime 4 is for a willing spirit. The Effect binds it to the object and turns it into a fetish belonging to the caster. So long as the caster keeps to their bargain with the spirit, all is fine.<br /> <br /> You can of course also use Spirit 4 to bind a willing spirit. Prime 4 is an overlap and workaround for mages who (for example) have Spirit 2 and can summon and bargain with a spirit, but lack Spirit 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still dont see that use of Prime 4. It implies somehow that Prime 4 could have some impact upon the Gauntlet, which I dont exactly agree.<br /> <br /> By the way, how to you handle with your &quot;Awakened Dagger&quot;, your mundane objects awakened using Spirit 3?<br /> <br /> I usually claim that those objects, besides the possibility to become attuned with you - meaning that they'll change with you if you shapeshift, they'll cross sideways with you, and they'll even have an astral reflection, floating toghether with you in astral form. To that, the item must share your ressonance - so, it must either be something that you truly value and is an old possession, or you must use Correspondence 3, Mind 2 or Prime 2 to attune it to you (Prime 2 is the faster and easier option).<br /> <br /> <br /> So, besides that, I claim that those small objects awakened with Spirit 3 becomes minor fetishes on their own sense, but they may grown in power as they grow in importance (awakened clothes would simply turn against anyone not the owner, but if the Mage uses constantly the same clothes - using Entropy 3 to make sure it is always clean as a way to please his T-shirt - than those clothes would become more powerful over time - maybe granting the Mage invisibility for example","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T04:47:51-08:00","id":1058894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058811#post1058811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how we've been handling it.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpirit 2 allows to you summon spirits and bargain with them. If the spirit is willing and has the Possession charm, it can enter an item and effectively become a fetish. The fetish doesn't have an owner and isn't specifically tied to the mage, but otherwise activates in the usual way. Of course, spirits with the Possession charm tend to be unpleasant, so be careful with your bargain.<br /> <br /> \u200bSpirit 4 is for binding an unwilling (or slumbering) spirit into a fetish. It forces them into the item and turns it into a fetish belonging to the caster. The spirit is likely to be unhappy unless the mage mollifies it somehow.<br /> <br /> \u200bPrime 4 is for a willing spirit. The Effect binds it to the object and turns it into a fetish belonging to the caster. So long as the caster keeps to their bargain with the spirit, all is fine.<br /> <br /> You can of course also use Spirit 4 to bind a willing spirit. Prime 4 is an overlap and workaround for mages who (for example) have Spirit 2 and can summon and bargain with a spirit, but lack Spirit 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I'll be using this sort of system. Thanks to my compulsive nature with regards to these things, it's either that or editing my M20 pdf with adobe acrobat.<br /> For my explanation of Prime 4, it's just reinforcing making the object's pattern mutable enough to accept supernatural power (as when creating a wonder), in this case the spirit's power rather than awakened magick. Not that I expect anyone else, even storytellers in my same gaming group, to do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T05:48:08-08:00","id":1058924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058843#post1058843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still dont see that use of Prime 4. It implies somehow that Prime 4 could have some impact upon the Gauntlet, which I dont exactly agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't see it that way, but YMMV <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. For Prime 4 to work in my game, the spirit needs to cross the Gauntlet first (or the mage does) - they have to be in the same realm, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058843#post1058843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, how to you handle with your &quot;Awakened Dagger&quot;, your mundane objects awakened using Spirit 3?<br /> <br /> I usually claim that those objects, besides the possibility to become attuned with you - meaning that they'll change with you if you shapeshift, they'll cross sideways with you, and they'll even have an astral reflection, floating toghether with you in astral form. To that, the item must share your ressonance - so, it must either be something that you truly value and is an old possession, or you must use Correspondence 3, Mind 2 or Prime 2 to attune it to you (Prime 2 is the faster and easier option).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI tend to rule that Awakened items (as well as fetishes and wonders) are automatically Consecrated to their creator - the process of Awakening or enchanting the item forges that resonant bond. Otherwise, yes, you have to forge that bond magically through whatever method you favour.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058843#post1058843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, besides that, I claim that those small objects awakened with Spirit 3 becomes minor fetishes on their own sense, but they may grown in power as they grow in importance (awakened clothes would simply turn against anyone not the owner, but if the Mage uses constantly the same clothes - using Entropy 3 to make sure it is always clean as a way to please his T-shirt - than those clothes would become more powerful over time - maybe granting the Mage invisibility for example</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI do something similar. Awakened items are treated like very simple artifacts, with one or two basic abilities. They can grow with time, as with your interpretation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058894#post1058894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I'll be using this sort of system. Thanks to my compulsive nature with regards to these things, it's either that or editing my M20 pdf with adobe acrobat.<br /> For my explanation of Prime 4, it's just reinforcing making the object's pattern mutable enough to accept supernatural power (as when creating a wonder), in this case the spirit's power rather than awakened magick. Not that I expect anyone else, even storytellers in my same gaming group, to do the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is my take. It's like making a Wonder.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:24:40-08:00","id":1058943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058924#post1058924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI don't see it that way, but YMMV <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. For Prime 4 to work in my game, the spirit needs to cross the Gauntlet first (or the mage does) - they have to be in the same realm, so to speak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, each to each's own<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058924#post1058924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI tend to rule that Awakened items (as well as fetishes and wonders) are automatically Consecrated to their creator - the process of Awakening or enchanting the item forges that resonant bond. Otherwise, yes, you have to forge that bond magically through whatever method you favour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I like the idea of having those &quot;personal fetishes&quot; as a Spirit 3, Prime 2 effect. Spirit is already a very powerful Sphere as it is, if I do that, it would allow spirit mages to awaken an item, consecrating it, and putting it to slumber again, that way getting several attuned items without Prime... It just seems too much to me (by the way, allowing Prime 4 to make fetishes ALONE also seems too much to me, just as much as requering both Spirit 4 and Prime 4 is too little)<br /> <br /> EDIT: besides, it is possible that you may wanna to awaken something, but not attuning it to you. If, for example, you're planning on gifting fetishes to others, it would be no good that Ted, the teddybear of your Verbena colleage, instead of having a strong attachement to the person which it shared its entire childhood, it became attuned with YOU instead...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","user":"AgentSmith","date":". 03-06-2017, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:30:00-08:00","id":1058945,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell from the terribly sparse 'Crafting Wonders' rules in M20 Prime 4 is mentioned because it is a design decision that you can't create Wonders without it. Thus it represents a bar that you must reach as a Mage before you can start building proper Wonders. There's also no difference in the crafting rules between Fetishes and Devices/Talismans - probably because they needed to cut down the space and are planning on publishing book on Wonders later on.<br /> <br /> There's no fluff in that section either so the justification for Prime 4 is pretty much absent, you've got to either roll with it or house rule it away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:38:10-08:00","id":1058950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058943#post1058943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... I like the idea of having those &quot;personal fetishes&quot; as a Spirit 3, Prime 2 effect. Spirit is already a very powerful Sphere as it is, if I do that, it would allow spirit mages to awaken an item, consecrating it, and putting it to slumber again, that way getting several attuned items without Prime... It just seems too much to me (by the way, allowing Prime 4 to make fetishes ALONE also seems too much to me, just as much as requering both Spirit 4 and Prime 4 is too little)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAs it happens, the only time this came up in our game, the character making the items had Prime 4 <i>and</i> Spirit 4, so it didn't really make much difference, lol. By the time the chronicle has reached that point, balance concerns become somewhat less relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058943#post1058943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: besides, it is possible that you may wanna to awaken something, but not attuning it to you. If, for example, you're planning on gifting fetishes to others, it would be no good that Ted, the teddybear of your Verbena colleage, instead of having a strong attachement to the person which it shared its entire childhood, it became attuned with YOU instead...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, good point. I'd say you can choose not to attune an item if you're planning to give it away. These things should be flexible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058945#post1058945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can tell from the terribly sparse 'Crafting Wonders' rules in M20 Prime 4 is mentioned because it is a design decision that you can't create Wonders without it. Thus it represents a bar that you must reach as a Mage before you can start building proper Wonders. There's also no difference in the crafting rules between Fetishes and Devices/Talismans - probably because they needed to cut down the space and are planning on publishing book on Wonders later on.<br /> <br /> There's no fluff in that section either so the justification for Prime 4 is pretty much absent, you've got to either roll with it or house rule it away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it only really mentions it in the Effects charts, making the distinction between willing and unwilling spirits. Earlier editions didn't have this distinction. I've found a way to incorporate it, but I'm not sure it's a very helpful distinction, as this thread shows <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:29:10-08:00","id":1058977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058945#post1058945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can tell from the terribly sparse 'Crafting Wonders' rules in M20 Prime 4 is mentioned because it is a design decision that you can't create Wonders without it. Thus it represents a bar that you must reach as a Mage before you can start building proper Wonders. There's also no difference in the crafting rules between Fetishes and Devices/Talismans - probably because they needed to cut down the space and are planning on publishing book on Wonders later on.<br /> <br /> There's no fluff in that section either so the justification for Prime 4 is pretty much absent, you've got to either roll with it or house rule it away.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forged by Dragon's Fire dont agree with that. Spirit Ways don't agree with that. Revised dont agree with that. Second Edition dont agree with that.<br /> <br /> This has been a (very) unfortunate new addition from M20, and one that is completely unecessary and unfriendly to the player. It just seems one of those disastrous attempts of game balance that truly breaks the game - who does have Prime 4 AND Spirit 4 anyway? Such a huge requirement is a ban to PC, besides, why will you take all the pain of Chiminage and all the spiritual trouble and the annoying spirit, that must be pleased otherwise can leave the item or act as a cursed one, why would you do one of those if you can make magikal items that will work as a fine hammer (instead of like a temperamental lamp djinn)?<br /> <br /> Also... Why is it needed such balancing? Is it really so necessary to make fetish manufacture even harder than already is?<br /> <br /> Thats a VERY frustranting change, first of all, it just weakens the Dreamspeakers, Verbena, Hermetics and Choristers A LOT, which in turn gives an even larger edgy to the Technomancers, specially the Technocracy (that has devices made with ONLY Prime out of their asses).<br /> Its a major disservice for the Mystical Traditions.<br /> <br /> For all those matters, Forged by Dragon's Fire have very good rules and fluffy, and should be considered as the primal source for those rules (not to mention that it is backep up by many other previous publications).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:33:27-08:00","id":1058981,"title":"","content":"&gt;specially the Technocracy (that has devices made with ONLY Prime out of their asses).<br /> The M20 rules for creating Wonders state that the Mage needs to know all the spheres in the effects they are going to craft into a Wonder<br /> <br /> and for the record I'm not overriding or contradicting any of the other rules I'm merely stating what I found in M20 so please don't get your nose out of joint","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:15:00-08:00","id":1059002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058981#post1058981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;specially the Technocracy (that has devices made with ONLY Prime out of their asses).<br /> The M20 rules for creating Wonders state that the Mage needs to know all the spheres in the effects they are going to craft into a Wonder</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is EXACTLY why the Technocracy is so op. There will ALWAYS be someone in the Union who knows how to do it; you just need to know how to ask it. The Technocracy dont work alone, as the solitary Hermetic working in his tower. The technocrats mass produce their stuff, so, anything that you could possibly need, they'll have.<br /> <br /> So yeah, making fetishes that much harder is weakning A LOT the already weaker Traditions (because they rely much more in fetishes than technocrats), not to mention that it ridiculously weakens the Dreamspeakers (and to lesser degrees, Verbena, Hermetics and Choristers)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058981#post1058981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and for the record I'm not overriding or contradicting any of the other rules I'm merely stating what I found in M20 so please don't get your nose out of joint</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not picking on you. My problem is with M20, not you. I was simply showing how this new addition contradicts everything that existed before - and how it were a terrible change","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:18:17-08:00","id":1059003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1058945#post1058945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can tell from the terribly sparse 'Crafting Wonders' rules in M20 Prime 4 is mentioned because it is a design decision that you can't create Wonders without it. Thus it represents a bar that you must reach as a Mage before you can start building proper Wonders. There's also no difference in the crafting rules between Fetishes and Devices/Talismans - probably because they needed to cut down the space and are planning on publishing book on Wonders later on.<br /> <br /> There's no fluff in that section either so the justification for Prime 4 is pretty much absent, you've got to either roll with it or house rule it away.</div> </div> </div> </div>It says &quot;or&quot; Prime 4 though not &quot;and&quot; Prime 4. So Prime 4 seems to be an alternative, not a necessity. Specifically it says:<br /> <br /> Spirit 4 (to bind unwilling spirit); or Prime 4 (willing spirit)<br /> <br /> And yes, this without any further explanation. Thus all this hooplah over it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Does it say Prime &quot;and&quot; Spirit in your books? (Maybe my friends messed around with my copy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-06-2017, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:55:54-08:00","id":1059048,"title":"","content":"It says Spirit 4 or Prime 4 in mine the same as the others - it's possibly a typo or something unintended, the only real way to find out is to ask the writers directly<br /> <br /> Regarding Technocracy vs Traditions - the Technocracy is only 'winning' if you choose to let them win in your campaign, Mage isn't a background that's set in stone, it's a flexible, choose your own menu, eat as much as you like buffet of ideas. The rules for making Wonders in M20 are the same for both factions so neither has an intrinsic advantage so allowing the Technocracy to 'mass produce' magic items is something that's down to the StoryTeller, not the rules.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if anything, the M20 rules <i>prevent </i>mass production because Wonders require tons of quintessence (5 per dot) which means either hundreds of Mages or ranked series of nodes feeding those production lines and that much shifting Quintessence is going to be pretty obvious too, thus drawing the attention of every supernatural predator around. So no, I don't think the Technocracy has any advantage or ability to mass produce under M20.<br /> <br /> Too many StoryTellers letting too many players get away with too much sh*t for too many years makes for this groundswell of assumption that the Technocracy is 'winning' or 'better'. It's always a choice, there's no fixed immovable rule that says how things must be in your game..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 03-06-2017, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:30:58-08:00","id":1059163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059048#post1059048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Technocracy vs Traditions - the Technocracy is only 'winning' if you choose to let them win in your campaign, Mage isn't a background that's set in stone, it's a flexible, choose your own menu, eat as much as you like buffet of ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true. This is actually cannon. Of course you can change whatever you like, but the cannon is that the Technocracy is winning by a very long shot (unless you dig all the Nephandic infiltration crap... But, disregarding the Nephandi, the Union has been winning by a very long time).<br /> So, you are free to change whatever you wanna. You can make the Technocracy be a group of aliens from out space, you can make the Traditions be interdimensional travellers.<br /> But thats not, however, the game's cannon. The cannon is, and it has always been, the Union kicking the Trads.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059048#post1059048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules for making Wonders in M20 are the same for both factions so neither has an intrinsic advantage so allowing the Technocracy to 'mass produce' magic items is something that's down to the StoryTeller, not the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong again. First of all, Technomancers Toybox lets the Technocrats (as well as VA and Etherites) make itens with Arete ratings without needing to sacrifice permanent Willpower; thats one advantage already.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the mass production of magikal devices by the Technocracy is part of the cannon lore of Mage. The Union mass produces them, and its it.<br /> <br /> There is nothing different with the rules about that; they simple produce magikal stuff in industrial scale, in assembly lines, instead of doing it like the traditionalists do, by artesanate work (the Technocratic Masters probably produce machines capable of produce only one single type of magikal Device... Like an enchanted machine that produces one blaster rifle an hour)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059048#post1059048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, if anything, the M20 rules <i>prevent </i>mass production because Wonders require tons of quintessence (5 per dot) which means either hundreds of Mages or ranked series of nodes feeding those production lines and that much shifting Quintessence is going to be pretty obvious too, thus drawing the attention of every supernatural predator around. So no, I don't think the Technocracy has any advantage or ability to mass produce under M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>LOL<br /> <br /> Do you have any idea of how powerful the Technocracy (or the Traditions, for that matter) really is? Have you ever read the Technocracy's Guide? <br /> <br /> Both Union and Traditions possess THOUSANDS of nodes... How do you think they can keep a HUGE Realm like Horizon?<br /> <br /> The Technocracy have (had) Mecha I and II, with the SOLE PURPOSE of being quintessence sources. And, the description of those Realms is &quot;produces an uncountable amount of quintessence&quot;.<br /> <br /> That thing about &quot;limited supplies&quot; is for the PC, not for the Union or Trad <u>as organization</u>. Do you think that Senex or Porthos beg a little tass for their spells? Those guys can get literally thousands of pieces of Tass in the blink of an eye.<br /> <br /> And the Union has even more.<br /> <br /> Why do you think the Technocrats have a background that allows them to request MAGIKAL DEVICES as needed for their missions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059048#post1059048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too many StoryTellers letting too many players get away with too much sh*t for too many years makes for this groundswell of assumption that the Technocracy is 'winning' or 'better'. It's always a choice, there's no fixed immovable rule that says how things must be in your game..</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no thing of &quot;ST's shit&quot;. Its cannon. It seems that its you that dont know all too well the game, perhaps you simply dont have some important suplements like The Techies guide and others, which is fine. You only need the Basic book, but this is the cannon scenario as Im telling you (thats actually said in the Basic books themselves however)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","user":"AgentSmith","date":". 03-06-2017, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T21:48:58-08:00","id":1059343,"title":"","content":"Look, technocrats employ a HUGE series of weird lab-built agents. Cloned &quot;Victors&quot;, Cyborgs, Hit Marks androids, and thats not to mention all that massive Primium they use on <i>everything</i>, and their most hardcore toys ever, their <i>Qui La Machine</i> freaking spaceships which basically are Primium flying fortresses filled with nuclear anti-matter cannons.<br /> <br /> Do you REALLY think they do all that in the back of their zen garden while they meditate to try to the moon to bless their machines?<br /> <br /> Why do you think that there are some many Union-only backgrounds that allows you to ask so many cool toys?<br /> <br /> Mass production of devices for the Union is a common thing. This is not &quot;STs shit&quot; at all, this is the most basic cannon of the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T22:05:59-08:00","id":1059347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059048#post1059048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Frankly, if anything, the M20 rules <i>prevent </i>mass production because Wonders require tons of quintessence (5 per dot) which means either hundreds of Mages or ranked series of nodes feeding those production lines and that much shifting Quintessence is going to be pretty obvious too, thus drawing the attention of every supernatural predator around. So no, I don't think the Technocracy has any advantage or ability to mass produce under M20.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>One last note: if you, for example, would look a veeeery old suplement, like &quot;Book of Chantries&quot;, you would get for example, all the <b>main</b> nodes (not all, mind you, just the bigger ones) that feed(ed) major Traditionalists and Techies' Realms, like Horizon, Doissetep, Autochtonia, etc. A major chapel like Doissetep, for example, had some dozens of what in M20 would be 5-10 nodes connected to it by ley lines, and probably hundreds of 1-4 nodes not described (just mentioned). A chantry like Doissetep could lose several of those Nodes without even noticing.<br /> <br /> About &quot;supernaturals noticing&quot;... Bah. Who cares. Places like Autochtonia are unbelivably tough strongholds. The massive attacks on Doissetep, Mus, Horizon... All that shit were a heavy crazy shit that the Union pulled, and it had a HUGE toll.<br /> <br /> Doissetep could withstand a massive Garou attack, for example... With little to fear (the techies attacked it with space ships and nukes, and still wasn't easy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T22:58:40-08:00","id":1059360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059163#post1059163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not true. This is actually cannon. Of course you can change whatever you like, but the cannon is that the Technocracy is winning by a very long shot...</div> </div> </div> </div>My Copy of the Revised edition at page 256 seems to say Technocratic Victory... (as one title) ... or Defeat? (as the other): which suggests there's more than one way to look at things. Also M20 clearly considers Technocratic victory a metaplot (not the only metaplot) and goes so far as to say - apparent technocratic victory. So an actual technocratic victory is hardly cannon. (They may just be screwing themselves over rather than winning is what page 256 seems to say)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 03-07-2017, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T00:38:22-08:00","id":1059377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059360#post1059360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My Copy of the Revised edition at page 256 seems to say Technocratic Victory... (as one title) ... or Defeat? (as the other): which suggests there's more than one way to look at things. Also M20 clearly considers Technocratic victory a metaplot (not the only metaplot) and goes so far as to say - apparent technocratic victory. So an actual technocratic victory is hardly cannon. (They may just be screwing themselves over rather than winning is what page 256 seems to say)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly - a much more insightful read of the text here <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. And M20 has done away with the idea of a restrictive canon (not <b>cannon</b>, lol) with its approach to the metaplot. It's up to individual STs to decide how they approach things. Just like it always was. M20 has just thankfully made it very clear. Good points all round <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T03:41:40-08:00","id":1059422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059360#post1059360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My Copy of the Revised edition at page 256 seems to say Technocratic Victory... (as one title) ... or Defeat? (as the other): which suggests there's more than one way to look at things. Also M20 clearly considers Technocratic victory a metaplot (not the only metaplot) and goes so far as to say - apparent technocratic victory. So an actual technocratic victory is hardly cannon. (They may just be screwing themselves over rather than winning is what page 256 seems to say)</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not FINAL VICTORY. There's a difference in there. The Technocracy, however, had always been in the winning side.<br /> <br /> This is, after all, the Technocratic reality. Or would you deny it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:08:18-08:00","id":1059483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AgentSmith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059422#post1059422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its not FINAL VICTORY. There's a difference in there. The Technocracy, however, had always been in the winning side.<br /> <br /> This is, after all, the Technocratic reality. Or would you deny it?</div> </div> </div> </div>My contestation is not with your assessment over their supremacy versus the traditions. That much has been part of the story from the beginning. What I'm pointing out is the word - winning - might not be completely accurate as to what is happening in the Technocratic Victory Metaplot in that their - winning - that scenario has actually given them a problem that may hinder their chances for true victory for decades to come.<br /> <br /> More importantly the main Metaplot in Mage Revised is no longer as cannon as it was in revised as noted by - That Damned Elusive Metaplot - sidebar in page 376 in M20 and the Future Fates sidebars throughout the book. That's all.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with an exceedingly powerful Technocracy and actually wish we were seeing more of a pickup from one of the Time of Judgement scenarios.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T10:03:23-08:00","id":1059589,"title":"","content":"&gt; This is, after all, the Technocratic reality. Or would you deny it?<br /> This is the really real world, maybe you need to take a chill pill<br /> &lt;backs away slowly&gt;<br /> <br /> <br /> One of my favourite lines because it's so totally meta on a couple of levels:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/name/nm0446314/?ref_=tt_trv_qu\" target=\"_blank\">T-Bird</a>: I knew I knew you, I knew I knew you. But you ain't you. You can't be you. We put you through the window. There ain't no coming back. <b>This is the really real world</b>, there ain't no coming back. We killed you dead, there ain't no coming back! There ain't no coming back! There ain't no coming back!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T11:07:48-08:00","id":1059615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059483#post1059483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My contestation is not with your assessment over their supremacy versus the traditions. That much has been part of the story from the beginning. What I'm pointing out is the word - winning - might not be completely accurate as to what is happening in the Technocratic Victory Metaplot in that their - winning - that scenario has actually given them a problem that may hinder their chances for true victory for decades to come.<br /> <br /> More importantly the main Metaplot in Mage Revised is no longer as cannon as it was in revised as noted by - That Damned Elusive Metaplot - sidebar in page 376 in M20 and the Future Fates sidebars throughout the book. That's all.<br /> <br /> I have no problem with an exceedingly powerful Technocracy and actually wish we were seeing more of a pickup from one of the Time of Judgement scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. So, I couldn't make myself clear, Im sorry.<br /> <br /> Lets say, the Technocracy is <u>more powerful</u> than the Traditions (or the weird alliance of the remnants outside the Trads). The Technocracy have a better organizational hierarchic system (its built as a military/governamental institution), they have more Nodes, more Tass, more Devices, more resources, more personal... Basically, they have more. Oh, and they have more of the Consensus either.<br /> <br /> That has always been the entire premisse of Mage from day 1 (when the Union were more of a rumor, and an agent were a fearsome thing, like the agents of the Matrix movie - you didnt fight them in 1st edition, you <i>ran</i>).<br /> <br /> Its up to the ST how powerful or how decadent they are, true. And, when playing a techie, players will find it terribly underpowered for all the shit they have to deal with.<br /> <br /> But in Mage, the basic premisse is that the Union is the bigger dog out there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:03:23-08:00","id":1059697,"title":"","content":"Yup. That's what makes the story interesting, even if you are a Traditions guy.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy as written forced me to think up all sorts of grand ideas that went well beyond what most people would think of in terms of magical tactics and combat, from illusionary projections of yourself that could actually deal psychic and real damage while you safely meditated in your sanctum, to the stormwarden grappler assassin who pulls enemies through the gauntlet from the other side of the umbra, to the legendary just good enough to be true guy with 5 in every attribute &amp; ability that mattered and the ability to dictate fate in his favor.<br /> <br /> It felt great to find ways to go toe to toe with the guys who tromped the tradition masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:52:58-08:00","id":1059724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1055893-fetish-information?p=1059697#post1059697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. That's what makes the story interesting, even if you are a Traditions guy.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy as written forced me to think up all sorts of grand ideas that went well beyond what most people would think of in terms of magical tactics and combat, from illusionary projections of yourself that could actually deal psychic and real damage while you safely meditated in your sanctum, to the stormwarden grappler assassin who pulls enemies through the gauntlet from the other side of the umbra, to the legendary just good enough to be true guy with 5 in every attribute &amp; ability that mattered and the ability to dictate fate in his favor.<br /> <br /> It felt great to find ways to go toe to toe with the guys who tromped the tradition masters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, the War of Ascension is a HUGE imagination exercise. The possibilities are staggering.<br /> <br /> How do a dreamspeaker Shaman fights? What tactics could he employ?<br /> <br /> How does the agents fight such a RD back?<br /> <br /> Furious Banes or Wyldlings insanely storming against the Men in Black? Does the land itself rises to fight those Technocratic abominations? Mud men rising from the ground, absurdly ancient monstruousities crossing dimensions to devour the technocrats...<br /> <br /> How do the agents deal with those threats? Do they send in their unholy artificial creation? Desecrate the works of the Mother by shielding this world from the Spirit? Do they unleash their Primal weapons on those ancient horrors to unmake them?<br /> <br /> And how those creepy Eutanathoi fight? Curses, mysterious murders, wraiths spies<br /> <br /> VAs hackers, Etherites with crazy machines, hermetics conjuring storms, cursed Verbena trees... Against monstruous ciborgs, unholy clones, nighmarish machines<br /> <br /> The possibilities both sides goes beyond imagination<br /> <br /> Which is why Mage is my favorite game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T14:38:04-08:00","id":1059758,"title":"","content":"An additional point to consider:<br /> The Techies may have more power, but can they use all that power at their leisure on the spot?<br /> <br /> What matters is the power you can bring to bear, not the total power you have.<br /> As written the Technocrats are spread out, working on countless things on countless locations.<br /> A single mystic can potentially screw them on one thing at a certain location.<br /> Both sides know very well that the threat of power has power itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}